<title>UNITED NATIONS: UN approves two more Iraq contracts, total at 26.</title>
<headline>UN approves two more Iraq contracts, total at 26.</headline>
<dateline>UNITED NATIONS 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.N. oil experts approved two additional crude contracts for Iraq under the oil-for-food accord, raising the number of approved contracts since the deal started on December 10 to 26, the U.N. said Wednesday.</p>
<p>No details on the contracts were released by the United Nations.</p>
<p>Terms of the oil deal allow Iraq to sell $2 billion worth of crude over a six-month period in order to buy food and supplies for civilians suffering from sanctions imposed on Baghdad after it invaded Kuwait in 1990.</p>
<p>--Patrick Connole, New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859 1620</p>
</text>
